### ============================================================
### Attendance deductions (mock §8 / §20 / §25).
///
/// The branch's Employees Performance → Deductions tab reads
/// GET /api/deduction-candidates/branch. That route runs the
/// attendance sweep first (1st of month → the gym's local today):
/// every derived absence and every stored Late/Absent day is
/// raised as a PRICED, pending DeductionCandidate — absence =
/// 3 × (base ÷ scheduled workdays), late = a quarter day — so
/// the list is never empty and never bare.
///
/// Run auth.http first (adminLogin). omarLogin below signs in
/// the seeded Branch Manager and picks his gym.
### ============================================================

### Branch Manager login + gym selection -> sets {{bmToken}}
# @name omarLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "omar@revive.hr",
  "password": "Revive!2026"
}

###
# @name omarSelectGym
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/select-gym
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "gymId": 1,
  "tempSessionToken": "{{omarLogin.response.body.tempSessionToken}}"
}

> {%
client.global.set('bmToken', response.body.accessToken);
%}

###
### ============================================================
### The tab's list — sweeps, then returns the priced rows.
### Run it twice: the sweep is idempotent per (employee, day),
### so the second read returns the very same rows.
### ============================================================

### Branch deductions (scoped to the BM's gym) -> 200 array
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/branch
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}

###
### Only one employee's rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/branch?employeeId={{employeeKarim}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}

###
### ============================================================
### The branch's decision on one row (Performance tab buttons).
### approve -> BranchApproved (goes to HR), reject -> final,
### edit -> re-prices while the status stays as it was.
### ============================================================

### Approve a row -> 200 { status: "BranchApproved" }
# @name branchApprove
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/branch-review
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approve"
}

###
### Re-price while approving (amount travels with the decision)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/branch-review
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "approve",
  "amount": 150
}

###
### Re-price only (edit) -> 200 with the new amount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/branch-review
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "edit",
  "amount": 250
}

###
### Reject -> 200 { status: "Rejected" } (final)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/branch-review
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "reject"
}

###
### ============================================================
### HR at month end (adminLogin): the queue of pending payroll
### lines, and the re-price — the review may carry the amount the
### sheet should actually charge; the line AND the candidate it
### materialized from both move to it.
### ============================================================

### Pending deduction lines -> 200 { items: [...] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates?status=Pending
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
### Accept at a revised amount (line + source candidate + totals)
# @name hrReview
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Accepted",
  "amount": 100
}

###
### Reject / waive it -> 400 when the amount is not positive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/1/review
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "Accepted",
  "amount": 0
}

###
### ============================================================
### Why a row can stand at 0: no salary source exists yet.
### The sweep prices (sheet covering the day → salary history →
### 0 + "No salary on file"). Record a salary and the very next
### read of the branch tab re-prices every still-pending row
### raised while nothing was on file — no manual entry, no new
### row (the branch's own edit/approve decisions are untouched).
### ============================================================

### Record Karim's salary -> 200 (salary history rung of the chain)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{employeeKarim}}/compensation
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "salary": 7800,
  "effectiveDate": "2026-10-01"
}

###
### The same rows again — now priced (3 × base ÷ workdays)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/deduction-candidates/branch?employeeId={{employeeKarim}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bmToken}}

###
### ============================================================
### The employee's own trail: candidates (priced) merged with
### legacy follow-ups, each with date / amount / status and any
/// correction request sitting on it.
### ============================================================

### Karim's deductions -> 200 array
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/employees/{{employeeKarim}}/deductions
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
